Floating point exceptions are misleadingly named; they also happen on
integer divide by zero. (NetHack 4 does use floating point calculations
when working out score, incidentally.) A trivial way to trigger a
floating point exception in vanilla: start a new healer in the
UNIX/Linux or DOS versions, and type

d4294967296$d4294967296$

and the game crashes with SIGFPE. (This is on the official bug list as
C343-337.)

